# Cloudflare Pages redirect rules. The deploy output is the repo root, so every committed file is otherwise
# served publicly. These paths are dev/build tooling and in-progress MWEB code that the live wallet never loads;
# redirect them to the app so they are not served from the production origin. (Pages _redirects has no 404
# status - only 301/302/303/307/308 - and a redirect is always followed even when the file exists, so a
# 302-to-root is the supported way to stop serving a committed file.)
#
# Kept intentionally public: tests.html / tests.js (a CSP-clean in-browser crypto self-verification
# page) and the vendored runtime deps.

/tools/*                    /  302
/mweb.mjs                   /  302
/mweb-test.html             /  302
/mweb-test.js               /  302
/vendor/noble-sha512.mjs    /  302
